e absolutely), and so \[ S_3 = \left(1- rac{1}{2^{m+1}}ight)  \sum_{k=1}^\infty  rac{1}{k^{m+2}}. \] It follows that \[ S_2 = \sum_{m=0}^\infty  rac{(-1)^m}{2^{m+1}} \sum_{k=1}^\infty  rac{1}{k^{m+2}} = \sum_{k=1}^\infty  rac{1}{2k^2} \sum_{m=0}^\infty \left(- rac{1}{2k}ight)^m = \sum_{k=1}^\infty  rac{1}{k(2k+1)} = 2 \sum_{k=1}^\infty \left(  rac{1}{2k} -  rac{1}{2k+1} ight) = 2(1-\ln 2). \] Finally, we have $S = S_1 + S_2 = 1$. 
